            "matched_text": "set aside",
            "start": 136,
            "end": 145
          }
        ],
        "text_preview": "On the aforesaid contentions,\nlearned counsel prays for allowing the revision and impugned judgments passed by both the Courts below be set aside and appropriate order may be passed."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "5c848de7f7604acb94b1cad6db177913_33",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "This Court has given its thoughtful consideration to the rival submission raised at bar."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "b2847c4d8d65438d90e7929dc0141745_34",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "It is undisputed that the sample was taken on 06/12/2007 and after completing procedural formalities complaint was filed against the applicant."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "8bb2aa549a6740e998d89f083c9134f9_35",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "From perusal of the evidence available on record, this Court is of the view that the conviction recorded by the Courts below cannot be interfered with NEUTRAL CITATION NO. 2024:MPHC-IND:31145 4 CRR-4242-2024 by way of this revision."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "7043cfd44c7040aa9c013830de654297_36",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\nHence, finding of conviction as recorded by the trial Court and affirmed by the Appellate Court is hereby affirmed."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "f292130af28b45778708a7cf0eb06a6c_38",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Submissions made on behalf of the applicant in alternative limb of the prayer for setting aside the jail sentence and imposing appropriate amount of penalty appears to be reasonable and has substance in light of the judgment by the Apex Cou"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "4bb5297d7b2747e4a232314edca3e58a_39",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "12. In case of Trilokchand (Supra) Hon'ble the Apex Court relying on T. Barai Vs. Henry Ah Hoe and Another 1948-1997 (1983) 1 F.A.C. (S.C.C.)177 has partly allowed appeal reducing the punishment for an offence under Section 16(1)\n(a) of the"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "05dcabab75ac40b08e87b131d756a3b8_40",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS",
          "explicit_leakage_phrase"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [
          {
            "pattern": "\\bset\\s+aside\\b",
            "matched_text": "set aside",
            "start": 98,
            "end": 107
          }
        ],
        "text_preview": "Giving benefit of reduce punishment under the Food Safety and Standard Act the Hon'ble Apex Court set aside sentence of 3 months imprisonment and enhanced a fine of Rs.500/- to Rs.5000/-."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "9e6b9bd8ae2d40fe906e27ce67b0409d_41",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "It is beneficial to reproduce paragraph 22 of the judgment T.Barai (Supra)\nrelied on which runs as under :-\n\"22."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "6c76c7556ecf432fa6be0aef86e4c7f8_42",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "It is only retroactive criminal legislation that is prohibited under Article 20(1)."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "880cfb1d754840628dc3a89acc288524_43",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "STA"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\nThe prohibition contained in Article 20(1) is that no person shall be convicted of any offence except for violation of a law in force at the time of the commission of the act charged as an offence prohibits nor shall he be subjected to a p"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "7c86670aa72b4f22af2dbe6a0a9873fa_44",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "It is quite clear that insofar as the Central Amendment Act creates new offences or enhances punishment for a particular type of offence no person can be convicted by such ex post facto law nor can the enhanced punishment prescribed by the "
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "17e08b933af848138d0b8e92577de629_45",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "But insofar as the Central Amendment Act reduces the punishment for an offence punishable under Section 16(1)\n(a) of the Act, there is no reason why the accused should not have the benefit of such reduced punishment."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "399fbfd1c09049fca158e63a61ff6462_46",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "The rule of Criminal Appeal No. 214/2016 etc. beneficial construction requires that even ex post facto NEUTRAL CITATION NO.\n2024:MPHC-IND:31145 5 CRR-4242-2024 law of such a type should be applied to mitigate the rigour of the law."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "75b5fa68e16f4dae86edf1d0c46f2b9a_47",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\nThe principle is based both on sound reason and common sense."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "c9b1d9e862f348a7bb31f49ed41fc6fc_48",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "This finds support in the following passage from Craies on Statute Law, 7th Edn., at pp. 388-89:A retrospective statute is different from an ex post facto statute."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "3f90b55650ef4965a3a357770a0c725c_49",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\"Every ex post facto law....\" said Chase, J., in the American case of Calder v.\nBull [1 L Ed 648 : 3 US 386 (1798)]"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "1e4e0ebed5824f49a7c19e726cef9f50_50",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\"must necessarily be retrospective, but every retrospective law is not an ex post facto law."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "6923f90ae7ee4f3cbdd4a77d0f9154fd_51",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Every law that takes away or impairs rights vested agreeably to existing laws is retrospective, and is generally unjust and may be oppressive; it is a good general rule that a law should have no retrospect, but in cases in which the laws ma"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "19314bd53fa14f239b4aa44b3fab3615_52",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "They are certainly retrospective, and literally both concerning and after the facts committed."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "b4726f004138493882ab8a39b7c131fd_53",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "But I do not consider any law ex post facto within the prohibition that mollifies the rigour of the criminal law, but only those that create or aggravate the crime, or increase the punishment or change the rules of evidence for the purpose "
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "a6f0a4ccfc8b4708b9e9422e6a1d578e_54",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "There is a great and apparent difference between making an unlawful act lawful and the making an innocent action criminal and punishing it as a crime.\""
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "87edc5f44e314414a8f78e5dccc6f455_58",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Co-ordinate Bench of this Court in Criminal Revision No.6276/2019 (Harish Dayani Vs. State of M.P. ) judgment dated 06/01/2020 relying on T.Barai (Supra) has also given the revisionist Harish Dayani the benefit of changes in law by substitu"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "535fdd91d1194bbd96f58383933ceb75_59",
        "summary_section": "decision",
        "labels": [
          "RPC"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:decision",
          "forbidden_labels:RPC",
          "suspicious_label:rpc"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\nThe sentence of rigorous imprisonment of 6 months with a fine of Rs.1000/- imposed on the revisionist under Section 7(i) r/w Section 16(1)(a)(i), 7(ii) r/w 16(1)(a)(i) and Section 7(v) r/w (i)\n(a)(ii) of the Act, 1954 has been substituted "
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "0146e6147db44c3f942cec449ce5a6f9_60",
        "summary_section": "decision",
        "labels": [
          "RPC"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:decision",
          "forbidden_labels:RPC",
          "suspicious_label:rpc"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "14. Keeping in view elucidation of law by Hon'ble the Apex Court and by the co-ordinate Bench of this Court, the submission made on behalf of the applicant on the point of sentence, deserves to be allowed."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "29283ec9ee974358b2fcec003565fabc_61",
        "summary_section": "decision",
        "labels": [
          "RPC"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:decision",
          "forbidden_labels:RPC",
          "suspicious_label:rpc",
          "explicit_leakage_phrase"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [
          {
            "pattern": "\\bset\\s+aside\\b",
            "matched_text": "set aside",
            "start": 190,
            "end": 199
          }
